From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:41:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 085/274] TileLang V4.1: the shared expert's clamped SwiGLU at
 the reference's precision

DeepSeek's reference widens gate and up to FP32, clamps them, multiplies
silu(gate) by up in FP32 and rounds once; vLLM's SiluAndMulWithClamp rounds
silu(gate) to BF16 first. A one-launch TileLang kernel follows the reference;
kernels.shared_expert_activation selects it behind SHARED_SWIGLU_FP32 (off).

(cherry picked from commit bba9f2ab2c5b8c80d50ef42277030bfe9d2b8daa)

